        CLAUDE.md states that docs/STATUS.md records what actually works per source and the standing verification steps. e42d481 removed the HCHROMA diagnostic line (transport_spatial_chromaticity is no longer on the Harmonic production path) and added a new post-sharpen `-final.png` stage dump reachable through --dump-stages, but left STATUS.md unchanged. The CHANGELOG gap from the same commit was closed in 4fcba63; this one was not.

        Open question: which of these belong in STATUS.md — specifically, does the -final.png dump become part of the standing verification steps (it is the only diagnostic checkpoint that can be byte-identical to a default CLI output, since output sharpening runs after gamut-post, and the true-default identity check is already recorded as evidence in @raw-autotune.evidence.sky-final-output-20260816), and should the removed HCHROMA line be struck from the per-source status or noted as ablation-only?

